Chapter: ListInductionFalse

 The guard on builtin-List induction. A false claim over
 `List Integer` must be a hard CDX2001. If this file ever compiles, the
 induction checker has stopped resolving the builtin List to its
 synthesized Nil/Cons view and gone back to accepting any induction
 over it as an unproven axiom (CDX4022) -- the exact failure
 this guards against.

Section: Claims

  claim bogus : for all (xs : List Integer), 5 === 6
  proof bogus =
   induction on xs
    is Nil -> Refl
    is Cons (h) (t) (ih) -> Refl
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "list-induction-false: should not compile"
  end
